cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Redivivus: Diablo II 1.14d reverse-engineered into buildable C++"
message: >-
  If you refer to Redivivus in writing, or build on the reconstruction, please cite it.
type: software
# Entity form rather than a person, to match how the project is credited elsewhere.
# Replace with given-names/family-names if you would rather be cited by name.
authors:
  - name: jaenster
    alias: jaenster
    website: "https://github.com/jaenster"
abstract: >-
  Diablo II: Lord of Destruction 1.14d recovered as C++ source that compiles, links and plays
  single player. The tree is generated from reverse-engineered Ghidra databases of the shipped
  Game.exe (Windows, plus the Intel Mac build from the same source revision) and organised by the
  module names the game itself uses. Correctness is checked by compiling the tree with Visual C++
  2005 SP1 and comparing the machine code of each function against the original binary, so a
  function that comes out byte-identical is evidence the decompilation was read correctly. The
  project is made to study and preserve the game; it is single-player only and contains no game
  data.
keywords:
  - Diablo II
  - reverse engineering
  - decompilation
  - matching decompilation
  - game preservation
  - Ghidra
  - "C++"
  - x86
repository-code: "https://github.com/jaenster/redivivus"
url: "https://redivivus.app"
